          "attribution": "Authored ideal-contact teaching case using the inherited Boolean rule; not historical measurements or construction instructions. Shannon (1938), sections I–II, uses the dual hindrance convention."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "binary-switch",
        "label": "Closed = 1; open = 0",
        "reading": {
          "text": "Use conduction states: a closed contact contributes 1; an open contact contributes 0. A complete conducting path makes the ideal permit lamp on (Y=1). This is the dual of Shannon’s hindrance notation, where 0 means closed and 1 means open. The earlier electromagnetic record motivates a controllable relay, but pulse observations alone do not prove that a real relay is an ideal instantaneous switch.",
          "attribution": "Authored ideal-contact teaching case using the inherited Boolean rule; not historical measurements or construction instructions. Shannon (1938), sections I–II, uses the dual hindrance convention."
        }
